+### HeteroPDDecider
+
+**Type:** `hetero-pd-decider`
+
+Decides per request whether to prefill on another pod or on the selected decode pod when prefill and decode pods run on different accelerator classes. Status: Alpha.
+
+#### What it does
+
+After the decode pod is selected, compares two estimates for the request's uncached tokens U:
+
+- Remote: `U / R_P + Q_P + U * kvBytesPerToken / bandwidth`, using the best prefill-capable pod.
+- Local: `U / R_D + Q_D`, plus a stall cost `N_D * U / R_D` weighted by `stallWeight`, where `N_D` is the number of requests running on the decode pod.
+
+R is the prefill throughput of the pod's accelerator class (from `profiles`), and Q is the waiting queue times `avgQueuedPromptTokens / R`. The remote estimate also adds `handoffOverheadMs`, and stall is scaled by `stallFraction`. Remote prefill runs when its estimate is within `ttftSLOMs` and lower than `(1 - safetyMargin) * (local + stallWeight * stall)`.
+
+Requests stay local when U is below `minUncachedTokens`, when decode KV usage is at or above `maxDecodeKVUsage`, when no compatible prefill pod exists, or when a pod carries the disable label. When the decode pod's class has no profile, the decider applies `fallbackNonCachedTokens` as a plain threshold.
+
+`strategy` selects how the decision is made:
+
+- `auto` (default): start from the stock rule (split when U reaches `stockNonCachedTokens`) and overrule it, in either direction, only when the estimates show the other path is cheaper by at least `overrideMargin`; an overruling split must also meet `ttftSLOMs`. Keep cost is `U / R_D + stallWeight * stall` and move cost is the remote estimate. The decode pod's own waiting queue is left out of both, because a remotely prefilled request waits for the same decode slot. When the decode pod or every prefill candidate lacks a profile, the stock answer stands. Reasons are `stock-split`, `stock-keep`, `override-keep` and `override-move` plus the shared vetoes.
+- `model`: the estimate comparison above, for every request.
+- `guarded-stock`: the stock rule, with vetoes only: a split is cancelled when the decode pod has at most `idleRunningRequests` running streams, an empty queue and a remote estimate no faster than local (`idle-veto`). It never splits a request the stock rule would keep.
+
+Requests stay local under every strategy when decode KV usage is at or above `maxDecodeKVUsage`, when no compatible prefill pod exists, or when a pod carries the disable label.
+
+Every decision increments `llm_d_epp_hetero_pd_decision_total{plugin_name, reason, remote_prefill}`. Per-request estimates are logged at DEBUG verbosity.
+
+#### How It Works
+
+The plugin is also a DataProducer. `Produce` runs before scheduling with all candidate endpoints and keeps the prefill-capable ones (`prefill`, `encode-prefill`, `prefill-decode`, `encode-prefill-decode` roles) with their current metrics. The decider reads that view because it only receives the selected decode endpoint.
+
+#### Inputs consumed
+
+- `PrefixCacheMatchInfo` on the decode endpoint, to subtract cached tokens. Missing info is treated as no cached prefix.
+- Tokenized prompt length.
+- Endpoint metrics: running requests, waiting queue size, KV cache usage.
+- Pod labels: accelerator class, KV compatibility key, disable flag.
+
+#### KV compatibility
+
+A split only works when the two pods can exchange KV: vLLM's NIXL handshake rejects pods that differ in model path, attention backend, KV layout and similar settings, and some layout mismatches produce wrong output instead of an error. The decider therefore treats compatibility as a hard rule, not a cost:
+
+- Pods carry a compatibility key in `compatibilityLabel`. Equal keys are compatible; different keys only through an approval, in one direction (prefill key to decode key), granted after the pair passed a validation run. Approvals come from `approvedPairs` entries `"prefillKey->decodeKey"` in the config, or live from labels `<acceptLabelPrefix><prefillKey>=true` on decode pods, which an approval controller can set and remove without restarting the router.
+- `compatibility: auto` (default): a missing key is accepted in a pool with one accelerator class, and treated as incompatible when the pool mixes classes. `strict` requires keys everywhere; `off` skips the check.
+- When prefill pods exist but none is compatible, the request stays local with reason `no-compatible-prefill`.
+- Failed handoffs exclude a pair: the plugin remembers which prefill/decode pair served each split request (`PreRequest`), counts a non-200 status or an error end of stream as a failure, and after `failureThreshold` failures in a row excludes the pair for `exclusionSeconds` (`llm_d_epp_hetero_pd_pair_exclusions_total`). A status code cannot tell a rejected handshake from other failures on that path; the threshold keeps one-off errors from excluding a pair.
+
+Add `hetero-kv-compat-filter` to the `prefill` scheduling profile so the prefill pod is picked with the same rule. It reads the decode pick that `disagg-profile-handler` publishes and keeps only compatible prefill endpoints, failing closed:
+
+```yaml
+- type: hetero-kv-compat-filter   # parameters: decider (default hetero-pd-decider)
+...
+schedulingProfiles:
+- name: prefill
+  plugins:
+  - pluginRef: prefill-filter
+  - pluginRef: hetero-kv-compat-filter
+
+#### Configuration
+
+##### Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `profiles` | none | Map of accelerator class to `{prefillTokensPerSec}`. |
+| `acceleratorLabel` | `llm-d.ai/accelerator-class` | Pod label holding the accelerator class. |
+| `compatibilityLabel` | `llm-d.ai/kv-compat-key` | Pod label holding the KV compatibility key. |
+| `fingerprintLabel` | `llm-d.ai/model-fingerprint` | Read as the compatibility key when a pod has no `compatibilityLabel`. |
+| `compatibility` | `auto` | `auto`, `strict` or `off`; see KV compatibility. |
+| `approvedPairs` | none | Key pairs `"prefillKey->decodeKey"` allowed although the keys differ. |
+| `acceptLabelPrefix` | `accept.kv-compat.llm-d.ai/` | Live approvals: a decode pod labelled `<prefix><prefillKey>=true` accepts KV from that prefill key. Empty disables. |
+| `speedLabel` | `llm-d.ai/prefill-tokens-per-sec` | A pod's own measured prefill speed, read live. It overrides the class profile for that pod, so a change of attention backend, vLLM build or card takes effect without editing `profiles` or restarting the router. A controller re-measures it when the pod's compatibility key changes. Empty disables. |
+| `failureThreshold` | `3` | Failed split requests in a row that exclude a pair. Zero disables exclusion. |
+| `exclusionSeconds` | `600` | How long an excluded pair stays excluded. |
+| `prefillProfile` | `prefill` | Scheduling profile whose pick is the prefill pod, used to track pairs. |
+| `disableLabel` | `llm-d.ai/hetero-pd-disabled` | A pod with this label set to `true` is excluded as prefill source and as remote-prefill destination. |
+| `kvBytesPerToken` | `131072` | KV bytes per token across all layers. |
+| `ttftSLOMs` | `0` | Remote estimates above this are rejected. Zero disables the check. |
+| `stallWeight` | `0.25` | Weight of decode stall seconds against time to first token. |
+| `safetyMargin` | `0.1` | Fraction by which remote must beat local. |
+| `maxDecodeKVUsage` | `0.9` | Decode KV usage at which requests stay local. |
+| `minUncachedTokens` | `256` | Requests with fewer uncached tokens stay local. |
+| `bandwidthGbps` | `10` | KV transfer bandwidth between classes. |
+| `sameClassBandwidthGbps` | `0` | Bandwidth between pods of the same class. Zero uses `bandwidthGbps`. |
+| `avgQueuedPromptTokens` | `1024` | Prompt tokens assumed per waiting request. |
+| `handoffOverheadMs` | `0` | Fixed cost of the remote path beyond the KV transfer: the sidecar's prefill request and response and the decode pod fetching the KV. Measure it as remote-path TTFT minus local TTFT for short prompts. |
+| `stallFraction` | `1` | Share of a local prefill's time that running streams lose, in [0, 1]. 1 is a full freeze; with chunked prefill it is much lower. |
+| `strategy` | `auto` | `auto`, `model` or `guarded-stock`. |
+| `overrideMargin` | `0.25` | How much cheaper the other path must be before `auto` overrules the stock rule. |
+| `stockNonCachedTokens` | `1024` | Stock threshold that `auto` and `guarded-stock` start from. |
+| `idleRunningRequests` | `2` | Running streams at or below which `guarded-stock` treats the decode pod as idle. |
+| `fallbackNonCachedTokens` | `1024` | Threshold used when the decode class has no profile. Zero keeps such requests local. |
+| `prefixMatchInfoProducerName` | approximate producer | Prefix producer whose match info is read. |
+
+##### Example
+
+See [`deploy/config/hetero-pd-epp-config.yaml`](../../../../../../../deploy/config/hetero-pd-epp-config.yaml).
+
+#### Limitations
+
+- The decider estimates from the best prefill pod; the prefill profile's own scorers may pick a different one.
+- Queue delay assumes `avgQueuedPromptTokens` per waiting request; it does not read per-request prompt lengths.
+- Bandwidth is static configuration.
+
+---
+
 ### AlwaysDisaggMultimodalDecider
 
 **Type:** `always-disagg-multimodal-decider`
